1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:04,335
Welcome to Night 6 of the Cognitive Shutdown Method.

2
00:00:04,285 --> 00:00:09,858
Tonight we combine everything you have learned into a single bedtime protocol.

3
00:00:09,858 --> 00:00:12,564
By now, your wake time is fixed.

4
00:00:12,564 --> 00:00:16,226
Your screens have stopped sixty minutes before bed.

5
00:00:16,226 --> 00:00:21,726
Caffeine, alcohol, and heavy meals are off the table for the evening.

6
00:00:21,726 --> 00:00:25,505
Your bedroom is cool, dark, and quiet.

7
00:00:25,505 --> 00:00:28,388
Your mind has been emptied onto paper.

8
00:00:28,388 --> 00:00:30,741
Tonight is about sequence.

9
00:00:30,741 --> 00:00:35,417
Each element you have learned matters, but the order matters more.

10
00:00:35,417 --> 00:00:39,182
The right sequence creates momentum toward sleep.

11
00:00:39,182 --> 00:00:42,064
The wrong sequence breaks the chain.

12
00:00:42,064 --> 00:00:51,947
Here is your protocol, starting ninety minutes before your wake time, minus eight hours, which gives your body the realistic sleep window.

13
00:00:51,947 --> 00:00:53,667
Ninety minutes out.

14
00:00:53,667 --> 00:00:55,358
Constructive worry.

15
00:00:55,358 --> 00:00:59,358
Brain dump on paper, problems left on the desk.

16
00:00:59,358 --> 00:01:01,138
Sixty minutes out.

17
00:01:01,138 --> 00:01:02,682
Screens off.

18
00:01:02,682 --> 00:01:04,564
Phone in another room.

19
00:01:04,564 --> 00:01:08,638
Switch to a book, stretching, or a warm shower.

20
00:01:08,638 --> 00:01:10,785
Forty-five minutes out.

21
00:01:10,785 --> 00:01:13,094
Lower the lights in the room you are in.

22
00:01:13,094 --> 00:01:14,932
Dim, not bright.

23
00:01:14,932 --> 00:01:17,638
Use lamps, not overheads.

24
00:01:17,638 --> 00:01:19,520
Fifteen minutes out.

25
00:01:19,520 --> 00:01:23,123
Brush teeth, bathroom, water by the bed.

26
00:01:23,123 --> 00:01:25,741
Final low-stimulation activity.

27
00:01:25,741 --> 00:01:26,932
Zero.

28
00:01:26,932 --> 00:01:29,329
Into the bedroom, into the bed.

29
00:01:29,329 --> 00:01:31,594
Cool, dark, quiet.

30
00:01:31,594 --> 00:01:33,123
Eyes close.

31
00:01:33,123 --> 00:01:34,270
That is it.

32
00:01:34,270 --> 00:01:35,785
Five steps.

33
00:01:35,785 --> 00:01:38,138
Same order every night.

34
00:01:38,138 --> 00:01:43,520
Your brain learns the sequence and prepares for sleep before you even lie down.

35
00:01:43,520 --> 00:01:46,711
Now let your body remember the sequence.

36
00:01:46,711 --> 00:01:48,535
Soften your hands.

37
00:01:48,535 --> 00:01:50,226
Soften your eyes.

38
00:01:50,226 --> 00:01:51,829
Soften your jaw.

39
00:01:51,829 --> 00:01:55,035
Breathe in slowly for four seconds.

40
00:01:55,035 --> 00:01:57,270
Hold gently for seven.

41
00:01:57,270 --> 00:01:59,652
Release through your mouth for eight.

42
00:01:59,652 --> 00:02:00,829
Again.

43
00:02:00,829 --> 00:02:02,299
In for four.

44
00:02:02,299 --> 00:02:03,902
Hold for seven.

45
00:02:03,902 --> 00:02:05,270
Out for eight.

46
00:02:05,270 --> 00:02:06,829
One last time.

47
00:02:06,829 --> 00:02:08,299
In for four.

48
00:02:08,299 --> 00:02:09,902
Hold for seven.

49
00:02:09,902 --> 00:02:11,270
Out for eight.

50
00:02:11,270 --> 00:02:13,476
The protocol is yours.

51
00:02:13,476 --> 00:02:14,814
Sleep well.

